🧬 What is Inheritance?
Inheritance is the mechanism in OOP that allows a class to acquire the properties and behaviors (methods) of another class.

📖 In simple terms:
"Child class inherits from Parent class"

🔑 Why Use Inheritance?
✅ Reusability of code

✅ Reduces redundancy

✅ Enables polymorphism

✅ Organizes classes hierarchically (IS-A relationship)

🧱 Types of Inheritance in Java
| Type             | Supported in Java? | Example                        |
| ---------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |
| **Single**       | ✅ Yes              | One class inherits another     |
| **Multilevel**   | ✅ Yes              | Class A → Class B → Class C    |
| **Hierarchical** | ✅ Yes              | One class → many child classes |
| **Multiple**     | ❌ Not with classes | Supported via **interfaces**   |


📦 Java Syntax
java
Copy
Edit
class Animal {
    void eat() {
        System.out.println("Eating...");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Barking...");
    }
}
Usage:
java
Copy
Edit
public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Dog d = new Dog();
        d.eat();   // from Animal
        d.bark();  // from Dog
    }
}
➡️ Dog is a child of Animal
➡️ Dog inherits the eat() method from Animal

📘 Real-World Analogy
Imagine:

Vehicle is a parent class

Car, Bike, Bus are child classes
They all share common features (like speed), but have their own specific behaviors.

🧠 Important Notes
Use extends keyword for class inheritance

Constructors are not inherited, but can be called using super()

Java does not support multiple inheritance with classes (to avoid diamond problem)

But you can implement multiple interfaces

✅ Interview-Ready Summary
| Question                                | Answer                                                           |
| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| What is inheritance?                    | Mechanism where one class inherits properties/methods of another |
| Keyword used?                           | `extends`                                                        |
| Does Java support multiple inheritance? | ❌ Not with classes, ✅ with interfaces                            |
| What is "super"?                        | Used to call parent class constructor or methods                 |
| What is IS-A relationship?              | `Dog` IS-A `Animal` — classic inheritance relationship           |
